Cloud Native Mail Service (CNMS)
Copyright 2026 Rocket Pad Platforms GmbH

This product includes software developed at Rocket Pad Platforms
(https://github.com/RocketPadPlatforms/cloud-native-mail-service).

CNMS is a control plane that manages well-known mail software (Postfix,
Rspamd, Dovecot, Valkey); those engines are distributed under their own
licenses (see docs/reference/third-party-licenses.md and the ADRs in
docs/decisions/ for the Go dependency report and version decisions).

The CNMS Postfix image links libpq (PostgreSQL License) for the
PostgreSQL map type and contains the Debian ca-certificates package
(MPL-2.0 root list, GPL-2+ scripts) as the system root certificates. The
data-plane images also contain BusyBox (GPL-2.0-only) and Debian base
packages, some of them under the GPL. They run unmodified as separate
programs and are not linked into the operator. See
docs/reference/data-plane-licenses.md for the components and licenses;
the versions are in internal/images/images.go.
